	"note": "Every value is a ceiling, and a row with no budget fails rather than passing. A Chromium ceiling is the worst of five 60 second runs of the whole matrix times 1.5, and those rows are marked `recorded`: they print and a breach is called out, but they do not fail the run. Five runs of the same matrix on one desktop disagreed with each other by more than that 1.5 on a different handful of rows every time, up to a row that stalled end to end, so a ceiling wide enough to hold them would say nothing and a tight one would fail on the weather. The nightly runner records its own; enforce these once it has. A replay ceiling is exactly what was measured and is enforced, because nothing in that lane can be unlucky.",
